* Fri Oct 02 2026 Dongkyun Son <dongkyun.s@samsung.com> - 1.0
- Build pigz from source and include it in the bootstrap
  MIC uses gzip -f to pack loop images into .tar.gz. Without pigz,
  single-core gzip is used, which is slow for large images
  (e.g. tizen-headed-aarch64 ~4.5GB). pigz enables parallel
  compression for faster image packing.
  pigz is not available as a Tizen package, so build from upstream
  source (v2.8) and install to bootstrap/bin/pigz after the bootstrap
  copy step. Source0 is the GBS auto-generated tarball; pigz source
  is provided as Source1 and extracted during %prep.

